    "id": "rate_half_bivariate_locator_extension_kernel_reduction",
    "title": "Locator-extension kernel reduction",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "dual Reed-Solomon interpolation criterion",
    "statement": "For each parameter coefficient of Q_Y(x)=A_x(Y)R_x(Y), X-degree at most rho is equivalent to the barycentric checks sum_(x in W) x^i q_j(x)/sigma'_W(x)=0 for 0<=i<|W|-rho-1. These checks define a linear matrix E_W on the deficiency-clone variables. Every actual endpoint failure has a blockwise-nonzero kernel for C_W=[M_W;E_W]. Full column rank of C_W excludes the pattern. The criterion controls extension on W only and does not impose the outside root sets or Hankel origin.",
